.TH FOREST-SESSION 1 "July 2026" "forest" "Forest desktop environment"
.SH NAME
forest-session \- Forest session manager
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B forest-session
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B forest-session
starts a Forest desktop session: it launches the window manager (xfwm4)
and any configured autostart entries, then starts the
.BR forest (1)
main process.
.PP
It is exec'd by
.IR /usr/share/forest/startforest ,
which is the xsession entry point registered for X11 display managers.
Users normally do not run
.B forest-session
directly; it is started automatically when a Forest session is selected
at login.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR forest (1)
